        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On &#x27;Zacharias, of the course of Abia... his wife was of the daughters of Aaron&#x27; (Lk 1:5), Cyril reads the doubled priestly pedigree (Zacharias by course + Elizabeth by lineage) as the canonical anchor of the New-Testament-emerging-from-the-Old-Testament-priesthood: the forerunner of the Lord is born to a fully-Aaronic family, the last priestly-house representative whose voice will yield to the One greater than himself. Tewahedo liturgical theology cites Lk 1:5 as the canonical anchor for the Aaronic origin of the Christian priesthood: the same priestly succession that Zacharias represented continues through Christ&#x27;s apostles into the Tewahedo episcopate.</p></aside>',
