        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>VIRGIN I</strong> n a prophecy concerning our Lord, Isaiah (7:14) says, “A virgin [R.V. marg., ‘the virgin’] shall conceive, and bear a son” (comp. Luke 1:31-35). The people of the land of Zidon are thus referred to by Isaiah (23:12), “O thou oppressed virgin, daughter of Zidon;” and of the people of Israel, Jeremiah (18:13) says, “The virgin of Israel hath done a very horrible thing.”",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
