        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>Simeon&#x27;s &#x27;Nunc dimittis&#x27; is for Cyril the canonical confession that the seeing of the infant Christ IS the seeing of salvation: the eyes that behold the babe have beheld the salvation God prepared &#x27;before the face of all peoples.&#x27; Cyril notes that Simeon does not say &#x27;I have seen one who will save&#x27; but &#x27;mine eyes have seen thy salvation&#x27; — the infant is the salvation, not merely its instrument. Tewahedo Compline preserves Nunc Dimittis as one of its earliest canonical-hymn anchors.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily IV (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
