        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>John&#x27;s &#x27;He shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost and with fire&#x27; is for Cyril the canonical disclosure that Christian baptism is fundamentally pneumatological — the water is the outer sign of an inner gift of the Spirit. The fire is not destruction but the purifying-and-illuminating fire of the Pentecostal descent. Tewahedo baptismal theology reads Lk 3:16 alongside Acts 2 as the canonical diptych of the Spirit&#x27;s outpouring in the New Covenant.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily VI (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
