        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>After reading from Isaiah, Christ declares &#x27;This day is this scripture fulfilled in your ears.&#x27; Cyril reads the synagogue homily as the canonical announcement that the Anointed-One&#x27;s program is the program of Is 61: good tidings to the poor, release to the captives, sight to the blind, acceptable year. Tewahedo public-reading lectionary still pairs Isaiah 61 with Luke 4 on Nazareth-synagogue feast days to preserve this Cyrillian fulfilment-arc.</p></aside>',
