        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>The voice from the cloud at the Transfiguration — &#x27;This is my beloved Son: hear him&#x27; — is for Cyril the canonical Father-Son disclosure made visible to Peter, James, and John. The Transfiguration is the proleptic glimpse of the post-Resurrection glory: the same flesh that walks the wilderness shines with the uncreated light. Tewahedo Transfiguration feast (Buhe) preserves Cyril&#x27;s reading of the divine voice as the canonical paternal attestation of the Son&#x27;s inseparable divinity.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily LI (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
