        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>Mary at Christ&#x27;s feet &#x27;hath chosen that good part&#x27; — Cyril reads the saying as the canonical anchor of contemplative priority: the service to the body (Martha) is necessary but the service to the Word (Mary) is the &#x27;one thing needful,&#x27; and Mary&#x27;s portion will not be taken from her. Tewahedo monastic theology cites Lk 10:42 as one of its earliest canonical anchors of the primacy of prayer and scripture-reading over outward works.</p></aside>',
