        "b",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s &#x27;Let your loins be girded about, and your lights burning&#x27; (Lk 12:35), Cyril reads the doubled-readiness-image (girded loins + burning lamps) as the canonical Lukan anchor of the vigil-of-the-Lord eschatological-posture: the Christian awaits the master&#x27;s return in the same posture as the Passover-Israelite (loins girded per Exo 12:11) and the wise virgins (lamps burning per Mt 25:1-13). Tewahedo Holy-Saturday vigil-liturgy cites Lk 12:35 + Exo 12:11 + Mt 25:1-13 as the canonical triple-witness for the vigil-of-the-Lord posture: the all-night Pascha vigil is the liturgical-iconic realization of this canonical readiness.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily XC (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD. Cf. Exo 12:11, Mt 25:1-13.",
