        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;This woman, being a daughter of Abraham, whom Satan hath bound, lo, these eighteen years, ought not she to be loosed from this bond on the sabbath day?&#x27; — Cyril reads Christ&#x27;s defence of the Sabbath healing as the canonical exposure of the Pharisaic perversion of the rest-commandment into a bondage. The Sabbath was made for the loosing of bonds, not for their maintenance. Tewahedo Sabbatical theology cites Lk 13:16 as the canonical anchor of the freedom-form of Sabbath rest.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily XCVI (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
