        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Whosoever doth not bear his cross, and come after me, cannot be my disciple&#x27; — Cyril reads the saying as the canonical anchor of voluntary martyrdom: the disciple&#x27;s own cross-bearing is the imitation that conforms him to the Master. The discipleship cost-calculation that follows (tower-builder, king-going-to-war) is the prudential prelude. Tewahedo monastic profession includes the voluntary embrace of the spiritual cross in direct dependence on this Cyrillian reading.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CIV (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
