        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>The publican standing afar off, smiting on his breast, saying &#x27;God be merciful to me a sinner&#x27; — Cyril treats this prayer as the canonical Lukan form of the Jesus-prayer: short, exact, self-acknowledging, mercy-petitioning. The publican goes down to his house justified, not the Pharisee. Tewahedo monastic prayer tradition preserves the publican&#x27;s prayer as the canonical seed of the continual prayer of the heart.</p></aside>',
