        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s citation &#x27;The stone which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner&#x27; (Lk 20:17, citing Ps 118:22), Cyril reads the stone-rejected-yet-cornerstone as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of the Christological-rejection-reversal: Christ is the rejected stone (by the Jerusalem builders) who becomes the foundation-cornerstone of the New-Covenant building (apostolic + Gentile-inclusion). The citation chain runs Ps 118:22 → Lk 20:17 → Acts 4:11 (Peter&#x27;s apostolic preaching) → 1 Pet 2:6-8 (foundation theology). Tewahedo ecclesiology cites this canonical chain as the foundation of the doctrine that the Tewahedo Church is built on Christ-the-Cornerstone, not on the rejecting Jerusalem-builders&#x27; approval.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CXXXIII (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD. Cf. Ps 118:22, Acts 4:11, 1 Pet 2:6-8.",
