        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s &#x27;Neither can they die any more: for they are equal unto the angels; and are the children of God, being the children of the resurrection&#x27; (Lk 20:36), Cyril reads the isaggelos (equal-to-angels) and the children-of-resurrection compound title as the canonical Lukan anchor of the resurrection-anthropology: the resurrected human is not made into an angel (against later Origenist confusion), but enjoys angelic immortality and angelic non-procreative communal-life. Tewahedo monastic theology cites Lk 20:36 as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine that the bahǝtawi&#x27;s celibacy anticipates the resurrection-state in this life — eschatological-existence proleptically embodied.</p></aside>',
