        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s prophecy &#x27;there shall not be left one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down&#x27; (Lk 21:6), Cyril reads the Temple-destruction prophecy as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of the canonical-end-of-the-Old-Covenant-cultus: the Temple as the chosen-place (Deu 12:5) is replaced by the eucharistic-altar in every local church. The destruction in 70 AD is the historical confirmation, but the spiritual transition is already accomplished in Christ. Tewahedo eucharistic theology cites Lk 21:6 + Heb 10 (sacrificial-system fulfilled in Christ&#x27;s one offering) as the canonical doubled-witness for the New-Covenant transition; the tabot bearing the Christic-presence replaces the Temple as the dwelling of God.</p></aside>',
