        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s &#x27;when ye shall hear of wars and commotions, be not terrified... the end is not by and by&#x27; (Lk 21:9), Cyril reads the not-by-and-by (ouk eutheōs — &#x27;not immediately&#x27;) qualification as the canonical Lukan anchor against eschatological-panic: military-and-political upheaval does NOT mean the end is now. Cyril notes the eschatological discourses regularly correct panic — Christian eschatology is patient, not feverish. Tewahedo eschatological-spirituality cites Lk 21:9 + 2 Th 2:1-2 (Pauline corrective against &#x27;the day of the Lord is at hand&#x27; panic) as the canonical doubled-witness for the doctrine of patient-eschatological-hope rather than panic-eschatology.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CXXXVIII (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD. Cf. 2 Th 2:1-2.",
