        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s &#x27;With desire I have desired to eat this passover with you before I suffer&#x27; (Lk 22:15), Cyril reads the Hebraic-redoubled-formula (epithymia epethymēsa) as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of Christ&#x27;s deliberate-eager-anticipation of the institutional Last Supper: not reluctant, not pressured, but deeply-desired. The Lord&#x27;s eagerness for the canonical-eucharistic-institution dignifies every later celebration. Tewahedo eucharistic theology cites Lk 22:15 as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of Christ&#x27;s desire-for-the-eucharist; every Tewahedo Mass is participation in the Lord&#x27;s own canonical-desire-fulfilment.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CXLIII (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD.",
