        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>PARADISE</strong> a Persian word (pardes), properly meaning a “pleasure-ground” or “park” or “king’s garden.” (See EDEN.) It came in course of time to be used as a name for the world of happiness and rest hereafter (Luke 23:43; 2 Corinthians 12:4; Revelation 2:7). For “garden” in Genesis 2:8 the LXX. has “paradise.”",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
