    (
        24,
        7,
        "a",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On the angels&#x27; recital of Christ&#x27;s pre-Passion prediction — &#x27;the Son of man must be delivered into the hands of sinful men, and be crucified, and the third day rise again&#x27; (Lk 24:7) — Cyril reads the dei (must-be) + third-day-rise as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine that the entire Passion + Resurrection sequence is divinely-necessary (the Lukan dei recurs at 9:22, 17:25, 22:37, 24:7, 24:26, 24:44 — six times the divine-necessity formula). The third-day-rise specifically fulfils Hos 6:2 + Jonah&#x27;s three-days. Tewahedo Pascha theology cites Lk 24:7 + Hos 6:2 + Mt 12:40 as the canonical triple-witness of the divinely-necessary third-day-resurrection.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CLV (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD. Cf. Hos 6:2, Mt 12:40.",
    ),
