        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On the risen Christ&#x27;s rebuke &#x27;O fools, and slow of heart to believe all that the prophets have spoken&#x27; (Lk 24:25), Cyril reads the rebuke + &#x27;all-that-the-prophets-have-spoken&#x27; as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of the comprehensive-prophetic-witness to Christ: the Resurrection-Christ holds his disciples accountable to ALL the prophets, not selected proof-texts. The slow-of-heart-to-believe formula appears as a Lukan refrain (Lk 24:11 + 24:25 + 24:38). Tewahedo Bibliology cites Lk 24:25 as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of the unitary-prophetic-canon: the Old Testament prophets uniformly witness to Christ; selectivity or hesitance is rebuked.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CLV (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD.",
