        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On the Emmaus-road exposition &#x27;And beginning at Moses and all the prophets, he expounded unto them in all the scriptures the things concerning himself&#x27; (Lk 24:27), Cyril reads the comprehensive-Christological-hermeneutic as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine that the entire Old Testament is Christologically interpretable: the Lord himself models the patristic-Christological hermeneutic on the resurrection road. Cyril&#x27;s own commentaries (and the entire patristic exegetical tradition) appropriate this canonical-resurrection-pattern as their methodological foundation. Tewahedo Andǝmta hermeneutic cites Lk 24:27 as the canonical Lukan anchor for the multi-layered Christological reading of the Tewahedo canonical Scriptures.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CLV (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD.",
